{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537368862,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzMTQ4NTA1Ng=="},"target":"70e6318e498023bb965c11c43a8cc892af56b608cc596d1ccfdad7d492f95079","message":"In a V6 repo, for a file under annex that has content present:\n\n```\nIn [5]: ds.repo.file_has_content('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[5]: False\n\nIn [6]: ds.get('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[6]: \n[{'action': 'get',\n  'message': 'already present',\n  'path': '/media/mih/C799-BE4A/test/studyforrest-data-structural_alt/sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w_defacemask.nii.gz',\n  'refds': '/media/mih/C799-BE4A/test/studyforrest-data-structural_alt',\n  'status': 'notneeded',\n  'type': 'file'}]\n\nIn [7]: ds.repo.file_has_content('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[7]: False\n```\n\n`get` works correctly, but `file_has_content()` is wrong both times.\n\nNow the same for a file that initially has no content:\n\n```\nIn [8]: ds.repo.file_has_content('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T2w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[8]: False\n\nIn [9]: ds.get('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T2w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[9]:                                                                                      \n[{'action': 'get',\n  'annexkey': 'MD5E-s152016--ef9df2a35bc7c08fe028653e2f9c9b1b.nii.gz',\n  'message': 'from mddatasrc...',\n  'path': '/media/mih/C799-BE4A/test/studyforrest-data-structural_alt/sub-01/anat/sub-01_T2w_defacemask.nii.gz',\n  'refds': '/media/mih/C799-BE4A/test/studyforrest-data-structural_alt',\n  'status': 'ok',\n  'type': 'file'}]\n\nIn [10]: ds.repo.file_has_content('sub-01/anat/sub-01_T2w_defacemask.nii.gz')\nOut[10]: False\n```\n\nIt gets it properly, but still reports the content absent afterwards. Any test that relies on this check will be a false positive failure.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537368689,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4NTUyODQ1NDY="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537368689,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4NTUyODQ1NTE="},"added":["annex-v6/7"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537368764,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMjgzNDM0Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2845#issuecomment-422834346"},"message":"Oh, and when this is being fixed, let's change the semantics of that function: It reports False for any file directly in Git -- which confuses me each and every time I have to use this.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537618291,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTg2MTU3NzE2Nw=="},"status":2}]}